---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const routes = [
  ['Start here', 'A short orientation to the problem of completed intelligibility and the three primitive dimensions.', '/theory'],
  ['Read the theory', 'The principal monograph, segmented into durable chapter routes for sustained reading.', '/theory'],
  ['Explore the 54-form atlas', 'See the 6 × 3 × 3 periodic architecture as an explorable coordinate system.', '/atlas'],
  ['Read the 54 expositions', 'Move cell by cell through plain-language accounts, manifestations, and coordinate-forced sentences.', '/forms'],
  ['Use the glossary', 'Browse preferred mature terminology, distinctions, theoretical levels, and cross-references.', '/glossary'],
  ['Follow the intellectual history', 'Trace the movement from sentence resolution to a constraint grammar of completion.', '/history'],
  ['Academic positioning', 'Read the disciplinary location, novelty claims, limitations, and proposed research programme.', '/academic'],
];
---
<BaseLayout>
  <div class="page">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">A periodic generative theory of transformation, completion, and persistence</p>
      <h1>Completed intelligibility, mapped.</h1>
      <p class="lede">A digital publication for reading and exploring a constraint grammar in which Transformation Pattern, Completion Topology, and Persistence Mode jointly generate fifty-four recurrent positions of completed form.</p>
      <div class="architecture" aria-label="Constraint grammar architecture">
        <div><strong>6</strong><span>Transformation Patterns</span></div>
        <div><strong>3</strong><span>Completion Topologies</span></div>
        <div><strong>3</strong><span>Persistence Modes</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Orientation</p>
          <h2>One theory, several reading modes.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The publication distinguishes the mature theory from its atlas, its fifty-four plain-language expositions, its terminological reference, and the documents that explain its development and academic position. These materials belong together, but they should not be flattened into one continuous document.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="route-grid">
        {routes.map(([title, body, href], i) => (
          <a class="route-card" href={href}>
            <small>{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</small>
            <h3>{title}</h3>
            <p>{body}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">The central distinction</p>
          <h2>Structure before crystallization.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The publication will preserve a governing distinction of the mature theory: coordinate-generated form → canonical crystallization → concrete manifestation. Atlas views and form pages will make those levels legible without collapsing them into interchangeable labels.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
